      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5aab30ea0b6da707273dbb98|full_name}: Reddit is one example, but I think there's some examples more analogous to VRChat.\nOverwatch, Final Fantasy XIV, and Dota 2 come to mind. After playing with someone, you can give commendations to other players. For being friendly, or helpful, or well-mannered. Basically, you can take the time to thank another player (without receiving something yourself).\n(There's slight differences in implementation: Commendations may be anonymous, the metrics may be private, and there may be rewards for being thanked often. )\nI think this serves two purposes: It encourages positive interaction, and gives players a reason to **celebrate** it. To feel good about their past interactions with other players.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
